// a7-glmr repro: parser error recovery can silently drop declarations.
// "good" parses first; the malformed import inside "main" triggers
// synchronize() (a7/parser.py:194,235) which restarts at the IMPORT token,
// discarding "main :: fn() {...}" wholesale. Observed with a7 @ 701c679:
//   exit 0, "Compiled ..." message, emitted .zig contains only good(),
//   no main entry point. Violates the fail-closed contract wording in
//   docs/SAFETY_CONTRACT.md ("must fail closed ... rejects the program").
// Variant without the leading "good" decl re-raises the ParseError (exit 5)
// because parser.py:174 only re-raises when zero declarations parsed so far.
good :: fn() {
    x := 1
}
main :: fn() {
    io :: import "std/io"
    io.println(42)
}
